IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc15-duties.l4 -- the regulative form of the duties, permissions and prohibitions of Part XIV (ss 468 to 482.1) in which the text names BOTH the party and the act:
-- the judge who may order another offence tried with a listed one (s 473(1.1)), the clerk who may adjourn (s 474), the court that may continue the trial of an accused who
-- absconds, adjourn it, continue it after adjourning and draw an inference (s 475), the court that shall not try an offence committed entirely in another province (s 478(1)),
-- the court or judge that shall determine an accused who pleads guilty to be guilty (ss 478(3), 479), the parties who shall comply with a case management direction (s 482.1(2))
-- and the court, justice or judge who may issue a summons or warrant (s 482.1(3)).
-- The criterion (the same for every provision of the range): a provision is written in this form where the text names the party and the act. Provisions that name no party
-- ("must be filed", "must be published", "shall not be withdrawn", "proceedings may be commenced") have none: no actor is invented (NOTES.md, fork: regulative-form). Deemings,
-- definitions, bars on proceedings and statements of jurisdiction are not duties and have no regulative form.
-- Each rule here has a decision-function twin in ccc15-general.l4, ccc15-venue.l4 or ccc15-rules.l4 that says whether the facts bring the case within the provision and that is asserted;
-- the rules here are run with #TRACE (tests: ccc15-tests-duties.l4). No period is invented: the text states none for any of them, so no rule carries WITHIN.
-- Imports the core only (`ccc-core`): the actors are the core's Party.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30).
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.

§ `Section 473(1.1) -- the judge may order that any offence be tried in conjunction`

-- src:8560 | Joinder of other offences
-- src:8561 | (1.1) Where the consent of the accused and the Attorney General is given in accordance with subsection (1), the judge of the superior court of criminal jurisdiction may order that any offence be tried by that judge in conjunction with the offence listed in section 469.
@ref s 473(1.1) (src:8560-8561)
DECLARE `s 473(1.1) act of the judge` IS ONE OF
    `s 473(1.1) order that any offence be tried by that judge in conjunction with the offence listed in section 469`

GIVEN `the consent of the accused and the Attorney General is given in accordance with subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 473(1.1) act of the judge`
`s 473(1.1) the judge's permission to order that any offence be tried in conjunction with the listed offence` MEANS
    IF `the consent of the accused and the Attorney General is given in accordance with subsection (1)`
    THEN PARTY `a judge`
         MAY `s 473(1.1) order that any offence be tried by that judge in conjunction with the offence listed in section 469`
    ELSE FULFILLED

§ `Section 474 -- the clerk may adjourn`

-- src:8564 | Adjournment when no jury summoned
-- src:8565 | 474 (1) Where the competent authority has determined that a panel of jurors is not to be summoned for a term or sittings of the court for the trial of criminal cases in any territorial division, the clerk of the court may, on the day of the opening of the term or sittings, if a judge is not present to preside over the court, adjourn the court and the business of the court to a subsequent day.
@ref s 474(1) (src:8564-8565)
DECLARE `s 474(1) act of the clerk` IS ONE OF
    `s 474(1) adjourn the court and the business of the court to a subsequent day`

GIVEN `the competent authority has determined that a panel of jurors is not to be summoned for the term or sittings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is the day of the opening of the term or sittings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a judge is not present to preside over the court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 474(1) act of the clerk`
`s 474(1) the clerk of the court's permission to adjourn when no jury panel is to be summoned` MEANS
    IF `the competent authority has determined that a panel of jurors is not to be summoned for the term or sittings` AND `it is the day of the opening of the term or sittings` AND `a judge is not present to preside over the court`
    THEN PARTY `the clerk of the court`
         MAY `s 474(1) adjourn the court and the business of the court to a subsequent day`
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- src:8566 | Adjournment on instructions of judge
-- src:8567 | (2) A clerk of the court for the trial of criminal cases in any territorial division may, at any time, on the instructions of the presiding judge or another judge of the court, adjourn the court and the business of the court to a subsequent day.
@ref s 474(2) (src:8566-8567)
DECLARE `s 474(2) act of the clerk` IS ONE OF
    `s 474(2) adjourn the court and the business of the court to a subsequent day`

GIVEN `the clerk acts on the instructions of the presiding judge or another judge of the court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 474(2) act of the clerk`
`s 474(2) the clerk of the court's permission to adjourn on the instructions of a judge` MEANS
    IF `the clerk acts on the instructions of the presiding judge or another judge of the court`
    THEN PARTY `the clerk of the court`
         MAY `s 474(2) adjourn the court and the business of the court to a subsequent day`
    ELSE FULFILLED

§ `Section 475 -- the court may continue the trial of an accused who absconds`

-- src:8568 | Accused absconding during trial
-- src:8569 | 475 (1) Notwithstanding any other provision of this Act, where an accused, whether or not he is charged jointly with another, absconds during the course of his trial,
-- src:8570 | (a) he shall be deemed to have waived his right to be present at his trial, and
-- src:8571 | (b) the court may
-- src:8572 | (i) continue the trial and proceed to a judgment or verdict and, if it finds the accused guilty, impose a sentence on him in his absence, or
-- src:8573 | (ii) if a warrant in Form 7 is issued for the arrest of the accused, adjourn the trial to await his appearance,
-- src:8574 | but where the trial is adjourned pursuant to subparagraph (b)(ii), the court may, at any time, continue the trial if it is satisfied that it is no longer in the interests of justice to await the appearance of the accused.
@ref s 475(1)(b) (src:8568-8574)
DECLARE `s 475(1)(b) act of the court` IS ONE OF
    `s 475(1)(b)(i) continue the trial and proceed to a judgment or verdict`
    `s 475(1)(b)(ii) adjourn the trial to await the accused's appearance`
    `s 475(1) continue a trial adjourned pursuant to subparagraph (b)(ii)`

GIVEN `the accused absconds during the course of the trial` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 475(1)(b) act of the court`
`s 475(1)(b)(i) the court's permission to continue the trial and proceed to a judgment or verdict` MEANS
    IF `the accused absconds during the course of the trial`
    THEN PARTY `the court`
         MAY `s 475(1)(b)(i) continue the trial and proceed to a judgment or verdict`
    ELSE FULFILLED

@ref s 475(1)(b)(ii) (src:8571-8573)
GIVEN `the accused absconds during the course of the trial` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a warrant in Form 7 is issued for the arrest of the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 475(1)(b) act of the court`
`s 475(1)(b)(ii) the court's permission to adjourn the trial to await the accused's appearance` MEANS
    IF `the accused absconds during the course of the trial` AND `a warrant in Form 7 is issued for the arrest of the accused`
    THEN PARTY `the court`
         MAY `s 475(1)(b)(ii) adjourn the trial to await the accused's appearance`
    ELSE FULFILLED

@ref s 475(1), the proviso (src:8574)
GIVEN `the trial is adjourned pursuant to subparagraph (b)(ii)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that it is no longer in the interests of justice to await the appearance of the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 475(1)(b) act of the court`
`s 475(1) the court's permission to continue a trial adjourned pursuant to subparagraph (b)(ii)` MEANS
    IF `the trial is adjourned pursuant to subparagraph (b)(ii)` AND `the court is satisfied that it is no longer in the interests of justice to await the appearance of the accused`
    THEN PARTY `the court`
         MAY `s 475(1) continue a trial adjourned pursuant to subparagraph (b)(ii)`
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- src:8575 | Adverse inference
-- src:8576 | (2) Where a court continues a trial pursuant to subsection (1), it may draw an inference adverse to the accused from the fact that he has absconded.
@ref s 475(2) (src:8575-8576)
DECLARE `s 475(2) act of the court` IS ONE OF
    `s 475(2) draw an inference adverse to the accused from the fact that the accused has absconded`

GIVEN `the court continues the trial pursuant to subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 475(2) act of the court`
`s 475(2) the court's permission to draw an adverse inference` MEANS
    IF `the court continues the trial pursuant to subsection (1)`
    THEN PARTY `the court`
         MAY `s 475(2) draw an inference adverse to the accused from the fact that the accused has absconded`
    ELSE FULFILLED

§ `Section 478(1) -- a court in a province shall not try an offence committed entirely in another province`

-- The text names the bearer ("a court in a province shall not try"), so the prohibition is derived from the answer of the decision function `s 478(1) a court in a province is barred ...`
-- (ruling N2 of 2026-11-04): the gate here is that answer being JUST TRUE.
-- src:8635 | Offence committed entirely in one province
-- src:8636 | 478 (1) Subject to this Act, a court in a province shall not try an offence committed entirely in another province.
@ref s 478(1) (src:8635-8636)
DECLARE `s 478(1) act of a court in a province` IS ONE OF
    `s 478(1) try an offence committed entirely in another province`

GIVEN `the court is barred from trying the offence, by s 478(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 478(1) act of a court in a province`
`s 478(1) the prohibition on a court in a province from trying an offence committed entirely in another province` MEANS
    IF `the court is barred from trying the offence, by s 478(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `the court`
         SHANT `s 478(1) try an offence committed entirely in another province`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "s 478(1): a court in a province tried an offence committed entirely in another province"
    ELSE FULFILLED

§ `Sections 478(3) and 479 -- the court or judge shall determine the accused who pleads guilty to be guilty`

-- src:8639 | Idem
-- src:8640 | (3) An accused who is charged with an offence that is alleged to have been committed in Canada outside the province in which the accused is may, if the offence is not an offence mentioned in section 469 and
-- src:8641 | (a) in the case of proceedings instituted at the instance of the Government of Canada and conducted by or on behalf of that Government, if the Attorney General of Canada consents, or
-- src:8642 | (b) in any other case, if the Attorney General of the province where the offence is alleged to have been committed consents,
-- src:8643 | appear before a court or judge that would have had jurisdiction to try that offence if it had been committed in the province where the accused is, and where the accused consents to plead guilty and pleads guilty to that offence, the court or judge shall determine the accused to be guilty of the offence and impose the punishment warranted by law, but where the accused does not consent to plead guilty and does not plead guilty, the accused shall, if the accused was in custody prior to appearance, be returned to custody and shall be dealt with according to law.
@ref s 478(3) (src:8639-8643)
DECLARE `s 478(3) act of the court` IS ONE OF
    `s 478(3) determine the accused to be guilty of the offence and impose the punishment warranted by law`

GIVEN `the accused consents to plead guilty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused pleads guilty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 478(3) act of the court`
`s 478(3) the court's duty to determine the accused to be guilty and impose the punishment warranted by law` MEANS
    IF `the accused consents to plead guilty` AND `the accused pleads guilty`
    THEN PARTY `the court`
         MUST `s 478(3) determine the accused to be guilty of the offence and impose the punishment warranted by law`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "s 478(3): the court did not determine the accused to be guilty and impose the punishment warranted by law"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- src:8648 | Offence outstanding in same province
-- src:8649 | 479 Where an accused is charged with an offence that is alleged to have been committed in the province in which he is, he may, if the offence is not an offence mentioned in section 469 and
-- src:8650 | (a) in the case of proceedings instituted at the instance of the Government of Canada and conducted by or on behalf of that Government, the Attorney General of Canada consents, or
-- src:8651 | (b) in any other case, the Attorney General of the province where the offence is alleged to have been committed consents,
-- src:8652 | appear before a court or judge that would have had jurisdiction to try that offence if it had been committed in the place where the accused is, and where the accused consents to plead guilty and pleads guilty to that offence, the court or judge shall determine the accused to be guilty of the offence and impose the punishment warranted by law, but where the accused does not consent to plead guilty and does not plead guilty, the accused shall, if the accused was in custody prior to appearance, be returned to custody and shall be dealt with according to law.
@ref s 479 (src:8648-8652)
DECLARE `s 479 act of the court` IS ONE OF
    `s 479 determine the accused to be guilty of the offence and impose the punishment warranted by law`

GIVEN `the accused consents to plead guilty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused pleads guilty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 479 act of the court`
`s 479 the court's duty to determine the accused to be guilty and impose the punishment warranted by law` MEANS
    IF `the accused consents to plead guilty` AND `the accused pleads guilty`
    THEN PARTY `the court`
         MUST `s 479 determine the accused to be guilty of the offence and impose the punishment warranted by law`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "s 479: the court did not determine the accused to be guilty and impose the punishment warranted by law"
    ELSE FULFILLED

§ `Section 482.1 -- case management`

-- src:8709 | Compliance with directions
-- src:8710 | (2) The parties to a case shall comply with any direction made in accordance with a rule made under subsection (1).
@ref s 482.1(2) (src:8709-8710)
DECLARE `s 482.1(2) act of a party` IS ONE OF
    `s 482.1(2) comply with the direction`

GIVEN party IS A Party
      `the direction was made in accordance with a rule made under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 482.1(2) act of a party`
`s 482.1(2) the party's duty to comply with the direction` MEANS
    IF `the direction was made in accordance with a rule made under subsection (1)`
    THEN PARTY party
         MUST `s 482.1(2) comply with the direction`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY party BECAUSE "s 482.1(2): the party did not comply with a direction made in accordance with a rule made under subsection (1)"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- src:8711 | Summons or warrant
-- src:8712 | (3) If rules are made under subsection (1), a court, justice or judge may issue a summons or warrant to compel the presence of the accused at case management proceedings.
@ref s 482.1(3) (src:8711-8712)
DECLARE `s 482.1(3) act of the issuer` IS ONE OF
    `s 482.1(3) issue a summons or warrant to compel the presence of the accused at case management proceedings`

GIVEN issuer IS A Party
      `rules are made under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 482.1(3) act of the issuer`
`s 482.1(3) the permission of a court, justice or judge to issue a summons or warrant to compel the presence of the accused` MEANS
    IF `rules are made under subsection (1)`
    THEN PARTY issuer
         MAY `s 482.1(3) issue a summons or warrant to compel the presence of the accused at case management proceedings`
    ELSE FULFILLED
